invariant: INV-68
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: rsa_sign64.c runs a signature's exponentiations on rsa_mont64_adx.c
  under CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX alone, so a session whose caller did not state that
  MULX runs in constant time multiplies the primes' words on it. Every byte
  stays right, so no vector notices. widemul.h sends no such value to the
  signer, so bin/x86_kernels_test also calls rsa_sign64_pss straight under
  each ch_cfg.cpu value and counts the calls into rsa_mont64_adx.c. The
  qemu lane runs it for x86-64.

--- old
    uint32_t both = CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY;
--- new
    uint32_t both = CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX;
